From: Omarchy psX contributors
Subject: [PATCH] addrlib: validate only the selected CI FMASK tile entry

Liverpool supplies a valid 2D FMASK entry at index14 and leaves index15
empty. HwlComputeFmaskInfo asserts both entries unconditionally, aborting
Firefox and Chromium when they allocate a2D multisample renderbuffer with
assertions enabled. The observed input was2D,128x16,eight samples.

Validate the selected entry at runtime before installing the temporary
output tile-info pointer. Missing or incompatible selected entries return
ADDR_INVALIDPARAMS; the2D layout algorithm and all other assertions remain
unchanged. An unused3D entry is no longer required for a2D request.

CPU-only public-API replay uses the captured Liverpool register tables.
No hardware acceptance is implied by this source change.

License: MIT; existing per-file notices remain unchanged.

---
--- a/src/amd/addrlib/src/r800/ciaddrlib.cpp
+++ b/src/amd/addrlib/src/r800/ciaddrlib.cpp
@@ -772,6 +772,17 @@
 
     AddrTileMode tileMode = pIn->tileMode;
 
+    // Liverpool leaves the unused 3D FMASK entry empty. Validate only the
+    // entry selected by this request, before borrowing the local tile info.
+    INT_32 tileIndex = tileMode == ADDR_TM_2D_TILED_THIN1 ? 14 : 15;
+    AddrTileMode fmaskMode = tileIndex == 14 ? ADDR_TM_2D_TILED_THIN1 :
+                                             ADDR_TM_3D_TILED_THIN1;
+    if ((static_cast<UINT_32>(tileIndex) >= m_noOfEntries) ||
+        (m_tileTable[tileIndex].mode != fmaskMode))
+    {
+        return ADDR_INVALIDPARAMS;
+    }
+
     // Use internal tile info if pOut does not have a valid pTileInfo
     if (pOut->pTileInfo == NULL)
     {
@@ -784,11 +795,6 @@
                 tileMode == ADDR_TM_PRT_2D_TILED_THIN1 ||
                 tileMode == ADDR_TM_PRT_3D_TILED_THIN1);
 
-    ADDR_ASSERT(m_tileTable[14].mode == ADDR_TM_2D_TILED_THIN1);
-    ADDR_ASSERT(m_tileTable[15].mode == ADDR_TM_3D_TILED_THIN1);
-
-    // The only valid tile modes for fmask are 2D_THIN1 and 3D_THIN1 plus non-displayable
-    INT_32 tileIndex = tileMode == ADDR_TM_2D_TILED_THIN1 ? 14 : 15;
     ADDR_SURFACE_FLAGS flags = {{0}};
     flags.fmask = 1;
 
